What are you guys' thoughts?

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:57.800
Should we have gotten a chess game before a video game adaptation of a game similar to chess?

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.580
I don't think so.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.040
I mean, I think that I'm surprised we haven't seen more tabletop-like games that utilize the

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.600
fact that it's a video game in an interesting way.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.840
Like chess, great, yeah, put it on the NES, but I can also just play chess.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.240
Whereas this is like, you couldn't do this.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.280
Like, it's nice to see something a little different than just what you can do on the tabletop.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:29.040
I also don't know how recently, like, computer-controlled chess was even possible.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:36.860
Like, I know that it was definitely in the 80s that it was like, oh, a computer can actually

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.300
play chess against a human and put up a fight.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.500
